<?xml version="1.1" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<databaseChangeLog xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
                   xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
                   xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">
    <!--
      recipe_tag.created_by was NOT NULL with no default, which made tagging a recipe impossible.
      Recipe maps tags as a plain @ManyToMany @JoinTable, so Hibernate's insert is
      `insert into recipe_tag (recipe_id, tag_id) values (?, ?)` - it has nowhere to put an audit
      value. RecipeIT proved it in Part 7a: "NULL not allowed for column CREATED_BY".

      Made nullable rather than dropped: the seeded rows hold real history. `created` needs no
      change - it is NOT NULL but defaults to CURRENT_TIMESTAMP. Auditing the association itself
      would mean promoting recipe_tag to an entity, as RecipeIngredient is; nothing reads these
      columns, so that was not worth it. Ported from my-recipes, which made the same fix.
    -->
    <changeSet author="jense" id="20261002-recipe-tag-created-by-nullable">
        <dropNotNullConstraint tableName="recipe_tag" columnName="created_by" columnDataType="VARCHAR(64)"/>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
